{
  "id": "os-296",
  "title": "How to Disable Cortana in Windows 10 - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Cortana is Microsoft’s built-in digital assistant designed to help users perform tasks using voice commands—such as setting reminders, searching the web, and managing productivity. However, due to low usage, privacy concerns, and performance issues, many Windows 10 users now prefer to disable or remove it entirely.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Here are the main reasons users disable Cortana:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>High Resource Usage:</strong></b><span> Runs constantly in the background, consuming RAM and CPU.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Privacy Concerns:</strong></b><span> Collects data for personalized recommendations.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>User Preference:</strong></b><span> Some prefer other assistants or none at all.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>Low Usefulness:</strong></b><span> Inconsistent voice recognition and inaccurate responses.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-1.png\" alt=\"Cortana_Img\" width=\"389\" height=\"620\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231110230144/Cortana_Img.png 389w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231110230144/Cortana_Img-100.png 63w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231110230144/Cortana_Img-200.png 125w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231110230144/Cortana_Img-300.png 188w\"><figcaption>Cortana</figcaption></figure><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Do you know?</strong></b><span> Cortana was named after the AI character in the famous video game </span><b><strong>Halo</strong></b><span> where it served as an AI assistant to the protagonist in the game. </span></p></blockquote><h2 id=\"how-to-disable-cortana-temporarily\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>How to Disable Cortana Temporarily</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Rather than completely removing </span><b><strong>Cortana </strong></b><span>you can disable it temporarily and here is how:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> Go to</span><b><strong> Windows Settings</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-2.png\" alt=\"Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic1\" width=\"768\" height=\"488\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002032/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic1.png 971w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002032/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic1-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002032/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic1-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002032/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic1-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002032/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic1-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002032/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic1-768.png 768w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Select </span><b><strong>Cortana</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-3.png\" alt=\"Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic2\" width=\"861\" height=\"484\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002033/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic2.png 861w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002033/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic2-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002033/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic2-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002033/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic2-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002033/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic2-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002033/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic2-768.png 768w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3: </strong></b><span>Turn off all available toggles (permissions, voice activation, etc.).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-4.png\" alt=\"Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic3\" width=\"548\" height=\"506\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic3.png 548w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic3-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic3-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic3-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-5.png\" alt=\"Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic4\" width=\"554\" height=\"321\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic4.png 554w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic4-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic4-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002035/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic4-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 4:</strong></b><span> Disable Cortana's access to microphone, location, and notifications.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-6.png\" alt=\"Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic5\" width=\"565\" height=\"678\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002036/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic5.png 565w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002036/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic5-100.png 83w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002036/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic5-200.png 167w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002036/Method1_Disable_Temporarily_Pic5-300.png 250w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 6:</strong></b><span> </span><b><strong>Restart your PC</strong></b></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">Note: Windows updates may re-enable some Cortana features automatically.</em></i></p></blockquote><h2 id=\"how-to-disable-cortana-permanently\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>How to Disable Cortana Permanently</span></h2><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span> </span><b><strong>Important:</strong></b><span> Create a </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-463\"><span>system restore point</span></a><span> before editing the registry.</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> </span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Press W</span><b><strong>indows+ R </strong></b><span>to open the Run dialog box and type </span><b><strong>regedit </strong></b><span>to open the registry editor.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-7.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic1\" width=\"458\" height=\"282\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002037/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic1.png 458w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002037/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic1-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002037/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic1-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002037/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic1-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Navigate to: </span><b><strong>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE</strong></b><span> to expand it.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-8.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic2\" width=\"424\" height=\"317\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic2.png 424w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic2-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic2-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic2-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Click on </span><b><strong>Software</strong></b><span> and expand it.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-9.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic3\" width=\"424\" height=\"420\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic3.png 424w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic3-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic3-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002038/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic3-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 4:</strong></b><span> Click on </span><b><strong>Policies</strong></b><span> and expand it.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-10.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic4\" width=\"363\" height=\"331\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002039/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic4.png 363w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002039/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic4-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002039/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic4-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002039/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic4-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 5:</strong></b><span> Select</span><b><strong> Microsoft </strong></b><span>under Policies.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-11.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic5\" width=\"377\" height=\"221\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic5.png 377w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic5-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic5-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic5-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 6:</strong></b><span>Right-click named </span><b><strong>Right-click</strong></b><span> on the right side of the screen and </span><b><strong>create a New Key</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-12.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic6\" width=\"756\" height=\"391\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic6.png 756w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic6-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic6-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic6-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002040/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic6-660.png 660w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 7:</strong></b><span> create a folder named </span><b><strong>Windows Search.</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-13.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic7\" width=\"306\" height=\"205\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic7.png 306w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic7-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic7-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic7-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 8:</strong></b><span> Select the </span><b><strong>Windows Search</strong></b><span> folder and click on the right side of the screen again and now click on</span><b><strong> the DWORD (32-bit</strong></b><span>Right-click</span><b><strong>) value</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-14.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic8\" width=\"484\" height=\"250\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic8.png 484w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic8-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic8-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002041/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic8-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 9:</strong></b><span> You will be allowed to create a file name as </span><b><strong>AllowCortana</strong></b><span>. Make sure you don't make any typing mistakes or else this will not work.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-15.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic9\" width=\"563\" height=\"164\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002042/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic9.png 563w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002042/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic9-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002042/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic9-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002042/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic9-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 10:</strong></b><span> Set the </span><b><strong>value data</strong></b><span> as 0 and click on ok. Here 0 = disabled and 1 = enabled.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-16.png\" alt=\"Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic10\" width=\"435\" height=\"230\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic10.png 435w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic10-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic10-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Method2_Disable_Permanently_Pic10-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 11:</strong></b><span> Restart your PC </span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Cortana will now be fully disabled.</span></li></ul><h2 id=\"how-to-reenable-cortana\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>How to Re-Enable Cortana</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>If you want Cortana back:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1: </strong></b><span>Open </span><b><strong>regedit</strong></b><span> (Windows + R → type regedit).</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-17.png\" alt=\"Enable_Cortana_Pic1\" width=\"458\" height=\"282\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004342/Enable_Cortana_Pic1.png 458w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004342/Enable_Cortana_Pic1-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004342/Enable_Cortana_Pic1-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004342/Enable_Cortana_Pic1-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Go to:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><code><span>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Search</span></code></li></ul><gfg-carousel><gfg-carousel-content alt=\"Enable_Cortana_Pic2.png\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251209121547892052/Enable_Cortana_Pic2.png\" width=\"424\" height=\"317\"></gfg-carousel-content><gfg-carousel-content alt=\"Enable_Cortana_Pic3.png\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251209121547770722/Enable_Cortana_Pic3.png\" width=\"424\" height=\"420\"></gfg-carousel-content><gfg-carousel-content alt=\"Enable_Cortana_Pic4.png\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251209121547683889/Enable_Cortana_Pic4.png\" width=\"363\" height=\"331\"></gfg-carousel-content><gfg-carousel-content alt=\"Enable_Cortana_Pic5.png\" src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251209121547637105/Enable_Cortana_Pic5.png\" width=\"377\" height=\"221\"></gfg-carousel-content></gfg-carousel><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Select the </span><b><strong>AllowCortana </strong></b><span>policy and set the value data as </span><b><strong>1.</strong></b><span> </span><b><strong>Here, 1 denotes enabled and 0 denotes disabled.</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-18.png\" alt=\"Enable_Cortana_Pic6\" width=\"537\" height=\"504\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004345/Enable_Cortana_Pic6.png 537w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004345/Enable_Cortana_Pic6-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004345/Enable_Cortana_Pic6-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118004345/Enable_Cortana_Pic6-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 4:</strong></b><span> Restart your PC.</span></p><h2 id=\"how-to-uninstall-cortana\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>How to Uninstall Cortana</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>If you want to uninstall Cortana and remove it completely from your PC, then follow the below steps:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> </span><b><strong>Go to Start </strong></b><span>Windows </span><b><strong>search for settings </strong></b><span>and open it.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-19.png\" alt=\"Uninstall_Cortana_Pic1\" width=\"942\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic1.png 942w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic1-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic1-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic1-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic1-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002043/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic1-768.png 768w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Click on </span><b><strong>Apps</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-20.png\" alt=\"Uninstall_Cortana_Pic2\" width=\"365\" height=\"361\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002044/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic2.png 365w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002044/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic2-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002044/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic2-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002044/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic2-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> Click on</span><b><strong> Installed apps</strong></b><span>.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-21.png\" alt=\"Uninstall_Cortana_Pic3\" width=\"589\" height=\"447\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002045/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic3.png 589w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002045/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic3-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002045/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic3-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002045/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic3-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 4:</strong></b><span> In the search bar,</span><b><strong> search for Cortana</strong></b><span>.</span></p><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-22.png\" alt=\"Uninstall_Cortana_Pic4\" width=\"633\" height=\"347\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002046/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic4.png 633w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002046/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic4-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002046/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic4-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002046/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic4-300.png 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 5:</strong></b><span> </span><b><strong>Click on the three dots</strong></b><span> on Cortana, a drop-down will appear, and then </span><b><strong>click on uninstall.</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/os-296-img-23.png\" alt=\"Uninstall_Cortana_Pic5\" width=\"785\" height=\"522\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002047/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic5.png 785w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002047/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic5-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002047/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic5-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002047/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic5-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002047/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic5-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20231118002047/Uninstall_Cortana_Pic5-768.png 768w\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2 id=\"why-cortana-failed\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Why Cortana Failed</strong></b></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Cortana never achieved the popularity Microsoft expected. Key reasons include:</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Strong competition from Siri, Alexa, and Google Assistant</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Outdated and limited user interface</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Poor marketing and slow updates</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>High memory usage that slowed down older systems</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>By 2023, Microsoft ended support for Cortana as a standalone Windows app.</span></p></div>",
  "textContent": "Cortana is Microsoft’s built-in digital assistant designed to help users perform tasks using voice commands—such as setting reminders, searching the web, and managing productivity. However, due to low usage, privacy concerns, and performance issues, many Windows 10 users now prefer to disable or remove it entirely.Here are the main reasons users disable Cortana:High Resource Usage: Runs constantly in the background, consuming RAM and CPU.Privacy Concerns: Collects data for personalized recommendations.User Preference: Some prefer other assistants or none at all.Low Usefulness: Inconsistent voice recognition and inaccurate responses.CortanaDo you know? Cortana was named after the AI character in the famous video game Halo where it served as an AI assistant to the protagonist in the game. How to Disable Cortana TemporarilyRather than completely removing Cortana you can disable it temporarily and here is how:Step 1: Go to Windows Settings.Step 2: Select Cortana.Step 3: Turn off all available toggles (permissions, voice activation, etc.).Step 4: Disable Cortana's access to microphone, location, and notifications.Step 6: Restart your PCNote: Windows updates may re-enable some Cortana features automatically.How to Disable Cortana Permanently Important: Create a system restore point before editing the registry.Step 1: Press Windows+ R to open the Run dialog box and type regedit to open the registry editor.Step 2: Navigate to: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE to expand it.Step 3: Click on Software and expand it.Step 4: Click on Policies and expand it.Step 5: Select Microsoft under Policies.Step 6:Right-click named Right-click on the right side of the screen and create a New Key.Step 7: create a folder named Windows Search.Step 8: Select the Windows Search folder and click on the right side of the screen again and now click on the DWORD (32-bitRight-click) value.Step 9: You will be allowed to create a file name as AllowCortana. Make sure you don't make any typing mistakes or else this will not work.Step 10: Set the value data as 0 and click on ok. Here 0 = disabled and 1 = enabled.Step 11: Restart your PC Cortana will now be fully disabled.How to Re-Enable CortanaIf you want Cortana back:Step 1: Open regedit (Windows + R → type regedit).Step 2: Go to:HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows SearchStep 3: Select the AllowCortana policy and set the value data as 1. Here, 1 denotes enabled and 0 denotes disabled.Step 4: Restart your PC.How to Uninstall CortanaIf you want to uninstall Cortana and remove it completely from your PC, then follow the below steps:Step 1: Go to Start Windows search for settings and open it.Step 2: Click on Apps.Step 3: Click on Installed apps.Step 4: In the search bar, search for Cortana.Step 5: Click on the three dots on Cortana, a drop-down will appear, and then click on uninstall.Why Cortana FailedCortana never achieved the popularity Microsoft expected. Key reasons include:Strong competition from Siri, Alexa, and Google AssistantOutdated and limited user interfacePoor marketing and slow updatesHigh memory usage that slowed down older systemsBy 2023, Microsoft ended support for Cortana as a standalone Windows app.",
